# Terminal recording of the scoring service. Render with:
#     vhs docs/demo.tape
#
# Records against the published image, so what the GIF shows is the artefact
# CI built and pushed, not a local build. --platform is required because the
# release image is linux/amd64 and this was recorded on Apple Silicon; on an
# amd64 host the flag is unnecessary.
#
# Payloads come from examples/, regenerated by scripts/make_examples.py, so
# the numbers on screen are reproducible rather than hand-picked.

Output docs/demo.gif

Set Shell bash
Set FontSize 14
Set Width 1280
Set Height 720
Set Padding 20
Set Framerate 20
Set TypingSpeed 35ms
Set Theme "Catppuccin Mocha"
Set WindowBar Colorful
Set WindowBarSize 40

# Setup: keep the recording focused on the API, not on a one-time image pull.
Hide
Type "clear && docker rm -f chrono >/dev/null 2>&1; docker pull -q --platform linux/amd64 ghcr.io/jonesrobm/chrono-sentinel:0.2.2 >/dev/null 2>&1; clear"
Enter
Sleep 5s
Show

Type "# Run the published image. No clone, no build."
Enter
Sleep 1s
Type "docker run -d --rm --name chrono --platform linux/amd64 -p 7860:7860 \"
Enter
Type "  ghcr.io/jonesrobm/chrono-sentinel:0.2.2"
Enter
Sleep 3s

Type "curl -s localhost:7860/readyz | jq"
Enter
Sleep 4s

Type "# A steady sensor reading -- the detector should be unexcited."
Enter
Sleep 1s
Type "curl -s localhost:7860/score -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \"
Enter
Type "  -d @examples/flat_window.json | jq"
Enter
Sleep 4s

Type "# A level shift: the machine-temperature failure signature."
Enter
Sleep 1s
Type "curl -s localhost:7860/score -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \"
Enter
Type "  -d @examples/step_change.json | jq"
Enter
Sleep 5s

Type "# 0.17 vs 0.93, each with its own Monte Carlo Dropout interval."
Enter
Sleep 3s

Hide
Type "docker rm -f chrono >/dev/null 2>&1"
Enter
